      "text": "<reasoning>The student has grasped the nuance of internal checks in parliamentary systems. Now I want them to apply this understanding to the practical outcome of governance, specifically legislation.</reasoning><state>Diagnosis</state><response>Exactly. Now, considering these two different structures—one with strict separation and one with fusion—how do you think this affects the ease with which laws are passed? For example, what happens when the executive and the legislative majority are from different political parties in each system?</response>"
